    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that a computed `customerCode` collision be resolved by appending `-<n>` (smallest `n \u2265 2`) to keep codes unique.\n\nI modified `AssignCustomerCode.java` (the pipeline step wired into `owners.POST.yml`):\n\n- Injected `OwnerRepository` (matching the existing pattern in sibling steps like `CountNamesakes`).\n- After computing the base code `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, it collects existing owners' `customerCode`s via `findAll()` (which, running before `SaveOwner`, sees only pre-existing owners) and, if the base collides, appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until unique.\n\nThe full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, including `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique`) passes: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nNote: since `HASH8` derives from normalized telephone + last name (and telephone uniqueness is enforced earlier in the pipeline), a real collision can't be forced black-box \u2014 the acceptance test asserts the uniqueness guarantee rather than the suffix directly, which the de-duplication logic upholds.",
